 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "The claimed proof manufactures far better numbers,",
   "start": 0.7,
   "end": 3.8
  },
  {
   "text": "from theta functions.",
   "start": 3.8,
   "end": 5.55
  },
  {
   "text": "Theta of t adds up e to the minus pi n squared t,",
   "start": 5.55,
   "end": 9.475
  },
  {
   "text": "over all integers n.",
   "start": 9.475,
   "end": 10.775
  },
  {
   "text": "It has a hidden mirror symmetry, which Riemann used to prove zeta's own.",
   "start": 10.775,
   "end": 15.075
  },
  {
   "text": "Functions with symmetries like this, called automorphic forms,",
   "start": 16.025,
   "end": 19.65
  },
  {
   "text": "can be carried from one symmetry group to a larger one by integrating against a",
   "start": 19.65,
   "end": 23.812
  },
  {
   "text": "theta function: a theta lift.",
   "start": 23.812,
   "end": 26.487
  },
  {
   "text": "Chain m lifts, take a special value called a period,",
   "start": 26.487,
   "end": 29.875
  },
  {
   "text": "and you get an algebraic number whose divisibility grows along the chain.",
   "start": 29.875,
   "end": 34.138
  },
  {
   "text": "In the note's analogy, each lift mimics one more order of multiplicity.",
   "start": 34.138,
   "end": 38.625
  },
  {
   "text": "How long a chain?",
   "start": 39.55,
   "end": 40.737
  },
  {
   "text": "Readers of the code describe two competing errors,",
   "start": 40.737,
   "end": 43.562
  },
  {
   "text": "roughly X over m, and m.",
   "start": 43.562,
   "end": 45.65
  },
  {
   "text": "They balance at m equals root X, leaving an error of about root X,",
   "start": 45.65,
   "end": 50.0
  },
  {
   "text": "the size the Riemann Hypothesis demands.",
   "start": 50.0,
   "end": 52.975
  },
  {
   "text": "Claude suggested root X.",
   "start": 52.975,
   "end": 54.5
  },
  {
   "text": "Alpöge's comment: and yet, what else could it be?",
   "start": 54.5,
   "end": 57.675
  }
 ],
 "cues": {
